course: dictionary
lesson: 11375
title: Abound: lots of something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To abound means to exist in large numbers or amounts. When something abounds, there is a lot of it, more than you might expect. «Rabbits abound in these fields» tells you there are many rabbits there.
explain: You can also say a place abounds in or with something. «The river abounds with fish» means the river has lots and lots of fish in it. The thing that is plentiful comes after in or with.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «has lots of» or «there are many». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning of abound.
fact: Abound means to exist in large numbers or amounts.
fact: «Abound in» and «abound with» both mean to have lots of something: «The forest abounds in birds.»
fact: «Rumours abounded» means people were saying lots of things.
fact: In formal writing, «Examples abound» means there are many examples.
fact: Abound is a verb, so its forms are abounds, abounded and abounding.
exercise: «Rabbits abound in these fields.» What does abound mean here? | Are made of wool | Are running away fast | Are very hard to find | *Exist in large numbers
exercise: «The river abounds with fish.» What does abounds with mean? | Has no fish at all | *Has lots of fish | Is dirty and grey | Is cold and fast
exercise: In the story, rumours abounded. What does this tell you? | The rumours were hidden in a box | *People were saying lots of things | Nobody said anything at all | Only one rumour was true
test: «The jungle abounds with monkeys and birds.» What does abounds with mean? | Has no monkeys | Is hot and sandy only | *Has lots of monkeys and birds | Was cut down last year
test: «Examples abound in this book, so you can see the idea clearly.» What does abound mean? | Are hard to find | Are written in red ink | *There are many | Are missing from the page
exam: «Ideas abound in the science club.» Which answer means the same as abound? | *Are plentiful | Are wrong | Are hidden | Are lost
